          deck: '36-card Swiss-German deck (6-10, Under, Ober, King, Ace).',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: "Deal 3 cards to each player and 3 cards face-down in the center ('The Window').",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Avoid having the lowest hand value (sum of cards in one suit) at the end of the round. Players start with 3 'lives'.",
          gameplay: "1. The dealer can swap their hand for 'The Window' before revealing it to the group.\n2. In turn, players can: - **Swap ONE**: Exchange one hand card with one center card. - **Swap ALL**: Exchange the entire hand. - **Pass**: Do nothing for the turn. - **Close (Knock)**: Signal the final round. All other players get ONE more turn.\n3. **Hosa Aba (31)**: If a player reaches 31, they reveal immediately and the round ends instantly.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hosa Aba.',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: - Only cards of the SAME SUIT are summed.',
            'Winning condition: Avoid having the lowest hand value (sum of cards in one suit) at the end of the round.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Always aim for 31 by collecting the Ace and two 10-value cards of the same suit. If you have 30.5 (three of a kind), it is a very strong defensive hand.',
          intermediate: 'Closing the round (Knocking) is a power move. Only do it if you have 25+ points and think others have much less.',
          advanced: "Watch what others take from the 'Window'. If an opponent takes a Rose, don't lead Roses unless you are dumping high cards you don't need.",
          tips: [
            'Collect Obers and Unders of the suit you have an Ace in.',
            "If the window has no cards of your suit, consider 'swapping all' to disrupt opponents' strategies.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
