          deckDescription: 'A 36-card German deck (Skat pack): four German suits with ranks Ace, King, Queen, Jack, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6. Used for Hosa Aba (Swiss-German variant of Schwimmen/31), a banking game where players aim for 31 in a suit.',
          suitDescription: 'The four German suits (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells) each contain nine cards. In Hosa Aba, matching suit is key: players swap or keep three cards to maximize the point total in one suit (Ace=11, face=10, pip=face value).',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks in each suit are Ace (11), King (10), Queen (10), Jack (10), 10, 9, 8, 7, 6. The goal is to hold three cards of the same suit totaling 31 (Ace+10+10) or the highest possible in one suit.',
